
==============================================================================
1. BOUND COVERAGE AND WIDTH, BY OFFSET BAND
==============================================================================

  L_sec is a LOWER bound on taxi implied by the next arrival at
  the same stand. What matters is not its width in absolute terms
  but how much it constrains RELATIVE to the offset in play.

  offset band                n     L>0     med L  med L/offset   % MSE
  [0, 1,800)           203,854    6.2%       298         0.25    30.7%
  [1,800, 3,600)        95,339    9.5%       357         0.14    26.5%
  [3,600, 7,200)        33,357    8.3%       341         0.07    18.5%
  [7,200, 14,400)        7,718    6.6%       355         0.04    13.7%
  >= 14,400              1,383    6.7%       321         0.02    10.1%

==============================================================================
2. DOES L_sec SEPARATE THE TWO ARMS? (offset >= 7200s)
==============================================================================

  pushed-late arm : n=8,898
  sat-at-stand arm: n=123

  metric                         pushed-late   sat-at-stand
  median L_sec                         0.000          0.000
  mean echo_prob                       0.005          0.559
  median actual_ground             7,858.000      7,685.000
  median inbound_arr_delay         3,902.000      2,642.000
  has_next                             98.7%          97.6%
  L_sec > 0                             6.7%           4.1%
  L_sec > 0.5*offset                    0.0%           0.0%
  L_sec > 0.8*offset                    0.0%           0.0%

  A large gap on the L_sec rows = stand occupancy is telling us
  which arm the flight is in, and the classifier isn't using it.

==============================================================================
3. WHAT WOULD USING THE BOUND BE WORTH?
==============================================================================

  clip pred up to L_sec  (link_confidence in ['high']):
    rows moved: 23   RMSE 337.6 -> 337.6  (+0.0s)

  clip pred up to L_sec  (link_confidence in ['high', 'med']):
    rows moved: 28   RMSE 337.6 -> 337.6  (+0.0s)

  sanity: true taxi < L_sec on 85/23,925 high-confidence rows (0.36%)
  (a low violation rate means L_sec is a trustworthy hard floor)
